{
  "baseCommit": "f5df207517d75a2dd6b00b43298b2e14ac019d94",
  "boundaries": [
    "A local native future target and its peer intentions are one atomic private GSFT record under the unchanged shared 32 MiB JOURNAL ceiling. No new image or wire/catalog frame is added.",
    "The independent new process matrix uses one actual stable-three EMPTY bootstrap and its first BARRIER. It derives original votes/application, all record/promotion states and complete interrupted/recovered file maps; it is not all-seven-profile or public-runtime acceptance.",
    "Eighteen halt/SIGKILL cases use 36 fresh JVMs and nine live lock probes. These are process crashes, not power loss.",
    "Final-source Java separately verifies normal reopening, six original-proof/backing-file refusals, missing-state refusal, duplicate intents and exact versus one-byte-short completion budget. That separate capacity/guard history is not included in the new independent process matrix.",
    "The final regression suites include fourteen additional peer-ledger process cases and actual selected-merge/lifecycle checks. The peer-ledger physical replay has eight evidence negatives; it is retained separately rather than counted as new future-target cases.",
    "The shared first-certificate Python helper was extracted without changing existing behavior; the prior finalized pending-publication evidence passes all six original negatives with the current reader, without rerunning that historical workload.",
    "Only the final isolated package is the 23-test current-source build. Earlier compile and ACK-ordering test-driver failures remain retained; no retries are relabelled as first-pass success.",
    "Future source capture intentionally refuses before a new promise until immutable propagation is implemented. Selection transfer, carried-entry recovery, governing future-target quorum, actual dispatch, autonomous offline-survivor continuation and full Phase 3 remain open.",
    "No push, PR, workflow, paid cloud execution, public membership enablement or V5.2 Runner change."
  ],
